    "summary": "This transaction involved the creation and manipulation of flash loans on Beanstalk Farms' governance system, ultimately leading to a successful exploit where nearly all of the treasury was transferred to the attacker's wallet.",
    "timeline_narrative": "The transaction began with the creation of two new accounts on the Beanstalk Farms contract. The attacker then used these accounts to request and receive flash loans from other protocols, which were deposited into the newly created accounts. The attacker then used this deposited value to gain control of the Beanstalk Farms governance system through an emergency commit function, allowing them to execute a proposal that transferred nearly all of the treasury to their wallet.",
    "root_cause_narrative": "The root cause of this exploit appears to be the lack of flash-loan resistance in the Beanstalk Farms governance system, which allowed the attacker to use the flash loan mechanism to gain control of the system and execute a malicious proposal. This is similar to the 'Beanstalk Farms' historical incident, where an attacker used a similar approach to drain the treasury.",
